-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part III (administration) and Schedules 1 and 2 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a worker, self-employed person, survivor, child or person with a disability who contributes to or may claim from the Canada Pension Plan
-- (one individual, one case), asking what Part III means for them: what the Minister must show them and how they can challenge it, whether and by when
-- they must apply for a Social Insurance Number or give it to an employer or report a new name, when they could be prosecuted, who may see
-- their information, what contribution rate the Schedules set, and when a change to benefits or rates can reach them.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the cp6-* modules as the questions that person would ask. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated:
-- every question builds the modules' records from plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates and choices from a list), each with an @desc worded as the
-- person would be asked, and calls the module's rule.
--
-- out of range (plain inputs here, as in the modules): section 6(1) (piece cp1); sections 30 and 33 (piece cp2); section 41(6) (piece cp2); sections 55 and 55.1 (piece cp3);
-- sections 81 and 82 (piece cp5); regulation 37(4), regulations 39 and 40 (piece cr2). The core's sections 2, 3 and 4 are imported, not restated.
--
-- WHAT THE SEAT DOES NOT ASK (NOTES.md has the reasons, row by row):
--   * the accounts of Canada and the Investment Board (ss 108(3) and (4), 108.1 to 111.1, 112, 115, 117, 118): a contributor cannot state a balance of
--     an account of Canada; the one fact about it a contributor can state (which account their contribution is paid into) is asked;
--   * the Governor in Council's regulation-making powers (ss 101, 107(3), 113.1(6), (11.144), (14)), which are inert in layer 1;
--   * the employer's side of s 98(5) (offence under s 102(3)): the employer is another party; the employee's side is asked (an employer seat is not written in this piece).
-- Where a rule turns on a judgment the text gives to an official ("it appears to the Minister that ..."), the question takes the judgment as a fact to be stated
-- ("if it appears to the Minister that ..."), and the @desc says so.
-- Where the Act leaves the answer to an agreement or a regulation that is not among the texts this encoding reads, the answer is NOTHING (shown as "not covered").
-- The contribution rates are those printed in Schedules 1 and 2 as deposited (current to 2026-09-30); an amendment under section 113.1 would change them.

§ `Part III -- administration of the Canada Pension Plan: the individual's questions`

-- Not a question: the four facts that make a person a "contributor" (section 2(1)), as one record, so that every question about the Record of Earnings asks them the same way.
GIVEN `made an employee's contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made a contribution on own self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `largest earnings contributed on in a year` IS A NUMBER
      `earnings attributed by a division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor`
`the facts that make me a contributor` `made an employee's contribution` `made a contribution on own self-employed earnings` `largest earnings contributed on in a year` `earnings attributed by a division` MEANS
    `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor` WITH
        `the person has made an employee's contribution` IS `made an employee's contribution`
        `the person has made a contribution on the person's own self-employed earnings` IS `made a contribution on own self-employed earnings`
        `the person's earnings on which a contribution was made, for each year, as in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)` IS LIST `largest earnings contributed on in a year`
        `earnings have been attributed to the person under section 55, 55.1 or 55.2` IS `earnings attributed by a division`

§§ `Who administers the Act, and what passes between the Ministers (sections 92 to 94)`

-- ss 91, 92(1), 92(2). The Minister of National Revenue has the control and direction of Part I (contributions); the Minister of
-- Employment and Social Development has it for everything else.
@export Which Minister has the control and direction of the administration of the part of the Act I am dealing with (s 92)?
GIVEN `my question is about contributions, which are in Part I of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your question about paying contributions (Part I of the Act)? Answer no for benefits and everything else.
GIVETH A Minister
DECIDE `Which Minister has control and direction of the part of the Act I am dealing with` IS
    `s 92 — the Minister with control and direction of the administration of the part`
        (IF `my question is about contributions, which are in Part I of the Act` THEN `Part I of the Act` ELSE `a Part of the Act other than Part I`)

-- s 92(2). The Minister of National Revenue must report to the Minister the information about earnings and contributions that the Minister needs.
@export If the Minister needs it, must the Minister of National Revenue report information about my earnings or contributions to the Minister (s 92(2))?
GIVEN `the kind of information` IS A `cp6 Kind of information the Minister of National Revenue reports to the Minister` @desc Which kind is it? One of: "earnings and contributions information needed for the Record of Earnings", "earnings information needed to determine a benefit or a financial adjustment", "statistical and other general information necessary for the administration of the Act", "information of another kind".
      `the information was obtained under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information obtained under the Canada Pension Plan Act (for example from your returns)?
      `the Minister requires it for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Minister (of Employment and Social Development) requires the information for the purpose of the kind you chose? This is the Minister's judgment; answer as the Minister has stated it.
      `it is necessary for the administration of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information necessary for the administration of the Act (for example for actuarial studies)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister of National Revenue report the information about me to the Minister` IS
    `s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` `the kind of information` `the information was obtained under the Act` `the Minister requires it for that purpose` `it is necessary for the administration of the Act`

-- s 92(3). A report for policy analysis, research or evaluation may be made available to the Minister despite any other Act or law.
@export May the Minister of National Revenue make a report available to the Minister for policy analysis, research or evaluation despite any other law (s 92(3))?
GIVEN `the report is made available by the Minister of National Revenue or a person that Minister designates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the report made available by the Minister of National Revenue or by a person that Minister has designated?
      `the report provides information necessary for policy analysis, research or evaluation related to the administration of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report provide information that is necessary for policy analysis, research or evaluation related to the administration of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the report be made available to the Minister despite any other Act or law` IS
    `s 92(3) — the report may be made available to the Minister despite any other Act or law` `the report is made available by the Minister of National Revenue or a person that Minister designates` `the report provides information necessary for policy analysis, research or evaluation related to the administration of the Act`

§§ `My Record of Earnings (sections 95 to 97)`

-- s 96(1). A contributor may apply for a statement of the earnings shown to their account in the Record of Earnings.
@export May I require the Minister to give me a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to my account (s 96(1))?
GIVEN `I have made an employee's contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ever made an employee's contribution to the Canada Pension Plan (had it deducted from your pay)?
      `I have made a contribution on my own self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ever made a contribution on your own self-employed earnings?
      `my largest earnings in a year on which a contribution was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In the year when it was greatest, how much of your earnings did a contribution count on, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `earnings have been attributed to me by a division of pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have unadjusted pensionable earnings been attributed to you under a division of earnings (sections 55, 55.1 or 55.2)?
      `I applied in the manner a regulation prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply in writing (or on the electronic form on the Internet) with the details regulation 39 requires?
      `an agreement with my province's pension plan governs how I get the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an agreement between the Minister and your province's pension plan (section 105) say how you get the statement? Answer no if you do not know of one.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I require the Minister to give me a statement of my earnings` IS
    `s 96(1) — a contributor's application obliges the Minister to furnish a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings`
        (`the facts that make me a contributor` `I have made an employee's contribution` `I have made a contribution on my own self-employed earnings` `my largest earnings in a year on which a contribution was made` `earnings have been attributed to me by a division of pensionable earnings`)
        `I applied in the manner a regulation prescribes`
        `an agreement with my province's pension plan governs how I get the statement`

-- s 96(1). If I am not satisfied with the statement I may ask the Minister to reconsider it.
@export May I ask the Minister to reconsider the statement of my earnings (s 96(1))?
GIVEN `I have made an employee's contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ever made an employee's contribution to the Canada Pension Plan (had it deducted from your pay)?
      `I have made a contribution on my own self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ever made a contribution on your own self-employed earnings?
      `my largest earnings in a year on which a contribution was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In the year when it was greatest, how much of your earnings did a contribution count on, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `earnings have been attributed to me by a division of pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have unadjusted pensionable earnings been attributed to you under a division of earnings (sections 55, 55.1 or 55.2)?
      `the Minister has given me a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister given you a statement of the earnings shown to your account?
      `I am not satisfied with the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not satisfied with the statement?
      `an agreement with my province's pension plan governs how I get the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an agreement between the Minister and your province's pension plan (section 105) say how you get the statement? Answer no if you do not know of one.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Minister to reconsider the statement of my earnings` IS
    `s 96(1) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the statement`
        (`the facts that make me a contributor` `I have made an employee's contribution` `I have made a contribution on my own self-employed earnings` `my largest earnings in a year on which a contribution was made` `earnings have been attributed to me by a division of pensionable earnings`)
        `the Minister has given me a statement`
        `I am not satisfied with the statement`
        `an agreement with my province's pension plan governs how I get the statement`

-- s 96(2). Sections 81 and 82 (reconsideration and appeal) apply to the request as though it were an application for a benefit.
@export Do the rules on reconsideration and appeal of a benefit apply to my request about my Record of Earnings (s 96(2))?
GIVEN `my request is made under subsection 96(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request a request under section 96(1), for a statement of your earnings or to reconsider one?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do sections 81 and 82 apply to my request as though it were an application for a benefit` IS
    `s 96(2) — sections 81 and 82 apply to the request as though it were an application for a benefit` `my request is made under subsection 96(1)`

-- s 97(1). An entry in the Record is final four years after the end of the year it was made in.
@export What is the last day on which I may question an entry in my Record of Earnings made in a year (s 97(1))?
GIVEN `the year the entry was made in` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year was the entry made? (for example 2020)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day on which I may question an entry in my Record of Earnings` IS
    `s 97(1) — the last day on which an entry may be called into question` `the year the entry was made in`

@export Can I still question an entry in my Record of Earnings made in a year, on a given day (s 97(1))?
GIVEN `the year the entry was made in` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year was the entry made? (for example 2020)
      `the day I want to question it` IS A DATE @desc On which day do you want to question the entry? (year-month-day, for example 2024-12-31)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still question an entry in my Record of Earnings on that day` IS
    `s 97(1) — an entry may be called into question on a day` `the year the entry was made in` `the day I want to question it`

-- s 97(2). The Minister may rectify the Record upwards, even after the four years.
@export If it appears to the Minister that the earnings shown to my account are less than they should be, may the Minister correct my Record of Earnings upwards (s 97(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister has information from the records of an employer, a former employer, an employee, a former employee or a person required to contribute on self-employed earnings, obtained after the four years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been given information from the records of an employer (or former employer, employee, former employee, or a person required to contribute on self-employed earnings) after the four years of section 97(1) had run?
      `it appears to the Minister for any other reason that the amount shown is too low` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Minister, for any other reason, that the amount shown to your account is less than it should be?
      `the amount shown to my account` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your account show, in dollars?
      `the amount that should be shown to my account` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you say, or the Minister has been told, that it should show, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister correct my Record of Earnings upwards` IS
    `s 97(2) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified upwards`
        `the Minister has information from the records of an employer, a former employer, an employee, a former employee or a person required to contribute on self-employed earnings, obtained after the four years`
        `it appears to the Minister for any other reason that the amount shown is too low`
        `the amount shown to my account`
        `the amount that should be shown to my account`

-- s 97(2.1). The Minister may remove an entry that is really a contribution to the provincial pension plan.
@export May the Minister remove an entry from my Record of Earnings that is really a contribution under my province's pension plan, on a given day (s 97(2.1))?
GIVEN `the information came from my province's pension plan under an agreement under section 105` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the information come from your province's pension plan under an agreement between the Minister and your province (section 105)?
      `it appears to the Minister that the entry relates to my contribution under the provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Minister that an amount shown to your account as a contribution under this Act relates instead to a contribution under the provincial pension plan?
      `the day the information was furnished` IS A DATE @desc On which day was that information furnished to the Minister? (year-month-day)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc On which day would the Minister authorize the removal? (year-month-day)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister remove the entry from my Record of Earnings on that day` IS
    `s 97(2.1) — the Minister may authorize the removal of an entry from the Record of Earnings on a day`
        `the information came from my province's pension plan under an agreement under section 105`
        `it appears to the Minister that the entry relates to my contribution under the provincial pension plan`
        `the day the information was furnished`
        `the day I ask about`

-- s 97(3). Another contributor's correction can reduce the earnings shown to my account.
@export Could the Minister reduce the earnings shown to my account because another contributor's earnings were increased (s 97(3))?
GIVEN `the other contributor's earnings were increased under subsection 97(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were another contributor's earnings in the Record increased under section 97(2)?
      `it appears to the Minister that the earnings with which that increase was made were shown to my account by mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Minister that the earnings and contributions behind that increase were incorrectly shown to your account?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could the Minister reduce the earnings shown to my account` IS
    `s 97(3) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified by a reduction of another contributor's earnings`
        `the other contributor's earnings were increased under subsection 97(2)`
        `it appears to the Minister that the earnings with which that increase was made were shown to my account by mistake`

@export What would be shown to my account after the Minister corrects it for another contributor's increase (s 97(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister makes the correction under subsection 97(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister make the correction?
      `the amount shown to my account` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your account show now, in dollars?
      `the part of the other contributor's increase that was shown to my account by mistake` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the other contributor's increase was shown to your account by mistake, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What would be shown to my account after the correction` IS
    `s 97(3) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the other contributor after any reduction`
        `the Minister makes the correction under subsection 97(3)`
        `the amount shown to my account`
        `the part of the other contributor's increase that was shown to my account by mistake`

-- s 97(4). If my earnings are reduced the Minister must tell me, in the prescribed manner; I may ask for reconsideration.
@export Must the Minister notify me if the earnings shown to my account are reduced (s 97(4))?
GIVEN `the earnings shown to my account are reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the earnings shown to your account been reduced (under section 97(3) or otherwise)?
      `the Record shows the Minister had told me the amount under section 96` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Record show that before the reduction the Minister had told you, under section 96, the amount of the earnings shown to your account?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister notify me of the reduction` IS
    `s 97(4) — the Minister must notify the contributor of the reduction` `the earnings shown to my account are reduced` `the Record shows the Minister had told me the amount under section 96`

@export Was the notice of the reduction of my earnings given in the prescribed manner (s 97(4))?
GIVEN `the Minister notified me in writing at my latest known address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister notify you of the reduction in writing, addressed to your latest known address (regulation 40)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the notice of the reduction given in the prescribed manner` IS
    `s 97(4) — the notice of the reduction was given in the prescribed manner` `the Minister notified me in writing at my latest known address`

@export May I ask the Minister to reconsider a reduction of the earnings shown to my account (s 97(4))?
GIVEN `the earnings shown to my account are reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the earnings shown to your account been reduced (under section 97(3) or otherwise)?
      `the Record shows the Minister had told me the amount under section 96` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Record show that before the reduction the Minister had told you, under section 96, the amount of the earnings shown to your account?
      `I am not satisfied with the amount of the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not satisfied with the amount of the reduction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Minister to reconsider the reduction` IS
    `s 97(4) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the reduction` `the earnings shown to my account are reduced` `the Record shows the Minister had told me the amount under section 96` `I am not satisfied with the amount of the reduction`

§§ `My Social Insurance Number (sections 98 to 100)`

-- s 98(1). Applying for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (after a separation, say) makes me apply for a number within thirty days, if I have none.
@export Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I applied for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (s 98(1))?
GIVEN `I applied for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 (for example after a separation)?
      `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already been assigned a Social Insurance Number?
      `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a Social Insurance Number assigned to you through your province's authority under an agreement between the Minister and the province (section 100)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I applied for a division` IS
    `s 98(1) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number`
        (`s 98(1) — subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` `I applied for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1`)
        (`an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province`)

@export By what date must I file my application for a Social Insurance Number because I applied for a division of earnings (s 98(1))?
GIVEN `the date I applied for the division` IS A DATE @desc On which day did you apply for the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings? (year-month-day, for example 2026-03-10)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I file my application for a Social Insurance Number because I applied for a division` IS
    `s 98(1) — the last day for filing the application` `the date I applied for the division`

-- s 98(2). Reaching eighteen and working in pensionable employment makes me apply within thirty days after the later of the two, if I have no number.
@export Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I have reached eighteen and work in pensionable employment (s 98(2))?
GIVEN `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service or apprenticeship?
      `I hold an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (the section 2(1) kind: a judicial office, a minister's office, a corporation director's position, or any other position with a fixed or ascertainable stipend)?
      `my employment is pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment pensionable employment (employment in Canada that is not excepted employment, section 6)?
      `I am or have become employed in it on or after reaching eighteen years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been employed in it on or after the day you reached eighteen years of age?
      `my employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in a province that has its own comprehensive pension plan (for example Quebec)?
      `the Act treats my employment as employment in another province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 4(2) treat your employment as employment in another province (for example because you are employed by the Government of Canada or an agent of it)?
      `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already been assigned a Social Insurance Number?
      `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a Social Insurance Number assigned to you through your province's authority under an agreement between the Minister and the province (section 100)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I have reached eighteen and work in pensionable employment` IS
    `s 98(2) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number`
        (`s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `I hold an office` `my employment is pensionable employment` `I am or have become employed in it on or after reaching eighteen years of age` `my employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `the Act treats my employment as employment in another province`)
        (`an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province`)

@export By what date must I file my application for a Social Insurance Number because I have reached eighteen and work in pensionable employment (s 98(2))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth? (year-month-day, for example 2000-03-15)
      `the day I became employed in pensionable employment` IS A DATE @desc On which day did you become employed in pensionable employment? (If you were already employed when you reached eighteen, give the day you started.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I file my application for a Social Insurance Number because I have reached eighteen and work in pensionable employment` IS
    `s 98(2) — the last day for filing the application` `my date of birth` `the day I became employed in pensionable employment`

-- s 98(3). A self-employed individual who must file a return and is not within (1) or (2) applies on or before the day the first payment is due.
@export Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number as a self-employed individual who must file a return of self-employed earnings (s 98(3))?
GIVEN `section 30 requires me to file a return of my self-employed earnings for a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 30 require you to file a return of your self-employed earnings for a year?
      `I applied for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1?
      `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service or apprenticeship?
      `I hold an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (the section 2(1) kind)?
      `my employment is pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment pensionable employment (employment in Canada that is not excepted employment, section 6)?
      `I am or have become employed in it on or after reaching eighteen years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been employed in it on or after the day you reached eighteen years of age?
      `my employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in a province that has its own comprehensive pension plan (for example Quebec)?
      `the Act treats my employment as employment in another province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 4(2) treat your employment as employment in another province?
      `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already been assigned a Social Insurance Number?
      `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a Social Insurance Number assigned to you through your province's authority under an agreement (section 100)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number as a self-employed individual` IS
    `s 98(3) — the individual must apply for a Social Insurance Number`
        `section 30 requires me to file a return of my self-employed earnings for a year`
        (`s 98(1) — subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` `I applied for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1`)
        (`s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `I hold an office` `my employment is pensionable employment` `I am or have become employed in it on or after reaching eighteen years of age` `my employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `the Act treats my employment as employment in another province`)
        (`an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province`)

@export By what date must I apply for a Social Insurance Number as a self-employed individual (s 98(3))?
GIVEN `the first day on or before which section 33 requires me to pay on my self-employed earnings` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day on or before which section 33 requires you to pay any amount on account of your contributions for that year? (year-month-day)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I apply for a Social Insurance Number as a self-employed individual` IS
    `s 98(3) — the last day for applying` `the first day on or before which section 33 requires me to pay on my self-employed earnings`

-- s 98(1), (2), (3). The application is filed in the form and manner that may be prescribed.
@export Is my application for a Social Insurance Number in the prescribed form and manner (s 98(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `the form is one the Minister authorizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form you used one that the Minister authorizes?
      `the manner is one a regulation prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply in the manner that a regulation prescribes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application for a Social Insurance Number in the prescribed form and manner` IS
    `s 98(1) to (3) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is in the prescribed form and manner` `the form is one the Minister authorizes` `the manner is one a regulation prescribes`

-- s 98(4). On my application the Minister must have a number assigned to me if I have none, and a Card may be issued.
@export If I apply for a Social Insurance Number, must the Minister cause one to be assigned to me (s 98(4))?
GIVEN `I have applied for a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a Social Insurance Number?
      `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already been assigned a Social Insurance Number?
      `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a Social Insurance Number assigned to you through your province's authority under an agreement (section 100)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to me` IS
    `s 98(4) — the Minister must cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to the individual`
        `I have applied for a Social Insurance Number`
        (`an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province`)

@export If I apply for a Social Insurance Number, may a Social Insurance Number Card be issued to me (s 98(4))?
GIVEN `I have applied for a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a Social Insurance Number?
      `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already been assigned a Social Insurance Number?
      `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a Social Insurance Number assigned to you through your province's authority under an agreement (section 100)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a Social Insurance Number Card be issued to me` IS
    `s 98(4) — a Social Insurance Number Card may be issued to the individual`
        `I have applied for a Social Insurance Number`
        (`an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province`)

-- s 98(5) and (6). My employer must ask me for my number; I must give it within thirty days after they ask.
@export Must my employer require me to tell them my Social Insurance Number (s 98(5))?
GIVEN `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service or apprenticeship?
      `I hold an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (the section 2(1) kind)?
      `my employment is pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment pensionable employment (employment in Canada that is not excepted employment, section 6)?
      `I am or have become employed in it on or after reaching eighteen years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been employed in it on or after the day you reached eighteen years of age?
      `my employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in a province that has its own comprehensive pension plan (for example Quebec)?
      `the Act treats my employment as employment in another province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 4(2) treat your employment as employment in another province?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer require me to tell them my Social Insurance Number` IS
    `s 98(5) — the employer must require the employee to inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number`
        (`s 2(1) — employment` `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `I hold an office` AND `my employment is pensionable employment`)
        (`s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` `I work under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `I hold an office` `my employment is pensionable employment` `I am or have become employed in it on or after reaching eighteen years of age` `my employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `the Act treats my employment as employment in another province`)

@export By what date must my employer require me to tell them my Social Insurance Number (s 98(5))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth? (year-month-day)
      `the day I became employed in pensionable employment` IS A DATE @desc On which day did you become employed in pensionable employment? (If you were already employed when you reached eighteen, give the day you started.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must my employer require me to tell them my Social Insurance Number` IS
    `s 98(5) — the last day on which the employer must require the employee to inform the employer` `my date of birth` `the day I became employed in pensionable employment`

@export Must my employer keep a record of my Social Insurance Number (s 98(5))?
GIVEN `my employer employs me in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer employ you in pensionable employment?
      `my employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in a province that has its own comprehensive pension plan (for example Quebec)?
      `the Act treats my employment as employment in another province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 4(2) treat your employment as employment in another province?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer keep a record of my Social Insurance Number` IS
    `s 98(5) — the employer must maintain a record of the employee's Social Insurance Number` `my employer employs me in pensionable employment` `my employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `the Act treats my employment as employment in another province`

@export Must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number when they require it (s 98(6))?
GIVEN `my employer has required me under subsection 98(5) to tell them my Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer required you, under section 98(5), to tell them your Social Insurance Number?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number` IS
    `s 98(6) — the employee must inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` `my employer has required me under subsection 98(5) to tell them my Social Insurance Number`

@export By what date must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number (s 98(6))?
GIVEN `the day my employer required me to tell them` IS A DATE @desc On which day did your employer require you to tell them your Social Insurance Number? (year-month-day)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number` IS
    `s 98(6) — the last day for the employee to inform the employer` `the day my employer required me to tell them`

-- s 99(1). The application is signed in my own hand, or by my mark before two witnesses if I cannot sign.
@export Is my application for a Social Insurance Number signed as the Act requires (s 99(1))?
GIVEN `I signed the application in my own hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you sign the application in your own hand?
      `I am unable to sign my own name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to sign your own name?
      `I made my mark on the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you attest the application by making your mark?
      `the number of witnesses who were present when I made my mark` IS A NUMBER @desc How many witnesses were present when you made your mark?
      `the witnesses' names and signatures are shown on the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the witnesses' names and signatures shown on the application?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application for a Social Insurance Number signed as the Act requires` IS
    `s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` `I signed the application in my own hand` `I am unable to sign my own name` `I made my mark on the application` `the number of witnesses who were present when I made my mark` `the witnesses' names and signatures are shown on the application`

-- s 99(2). A change of name must be reported to the Minister within sixty days, unless I have already told another authority empowered to receive it.
@export Must I tell the Minister my new name, and by what date (s 99(2))?
GIVEN `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been assigned a Social Insurance Number?
      `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your Social Insurance Number assigned through your province's authority under an agreement (section 100)?
      `I have already told another authority empowered to receive my new name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already told another authority that is empowered to receive that information about your new name?
      `the day my change of name became effective` IS A DATE @desc On which day did your change of name become effective? (year-month-day)
      `I worked that day under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, were you working under a contract of service or apprenticeship?
      `I held an office that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, did you hold an office (the section 2(1) kind)?
      `my work that day was pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that employment pensionable employment (section 6)?
      `that employment was in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that employment in a province that has its own comprehensive pension plan (for example Quebec)?
      `the Act treated that employment as employment in another province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did section 4(2) treat that employment as employment in another province?
      `I later became employed in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you later become employed in pensionable employment (after the change of name, when you were not so employed that day)?
      `the day I later became employed in pensionable employment` IS A DATE @desc If so, on which day? (year-month-day; any date if you answered no)
      `I am required to pay on my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required under section 33 to pay an amount on account of the contributions on your self-employed earnings?
      `the first day on or before which section 33 requires me to pay` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first day on or before which you are required to pay? (year-month-day; any date if you answered no)
GIVETH A `cp6 Time for informing the Minister of a change of name`
DECIDE `Must I tell the Minister my new name and by what date` IS
    `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name`
        (`an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` `a number was assigned to me under the authority of an Act of Parliament` `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to me under an agreement with my province`)
        `I have already told another authority empowered to receive my new name`
        `the day my change of name became effective`
        `I was employed in pensionable employment that day`
        `my later employment day`
        `my first payment day`
    WHERE
        -- employed in pensionable employment within the reach of Part III (section 4(1)(a), fork C6-F14)
        `I was employed in pensionable employment that day` MEANS
                `s 2(1) — employment` `I worked that day under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `I held an office that day`
            AND `my work that day was pensionable employment`
            AND `s 4(1)(a) — the Act's provisions on employee and employer contributions reach the employment` `that employment was in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `the Act treated that employment as employment in another province`
        `my later employment day` MEANS
            IF `I later became employed in pensionable employment` THEN JUST `the day I later became employed in pensionable employment` ELSE NOTHING
        `my first payment day` MEANS
            IF `I am required to pay on my self-employed earnings` THEN JUST `the first day on or before which section 33 requires me to pay` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 100(2). A number assigned through a province under an agreement counts as assigned under this Act.
@export Is a Social Insurance Number assigned to me through my province's authority treated as assigned under this Act (s 100(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister caused the number to be assigned under an agreement with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your Social Insurance Number assigned through your province's authority under an agreement between the Minister and the province (section 100(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a number assigned through my province's authority treated as assigned under this Act` IS
    `s 100(2) — a number caused to be assigned under an agreement is deemed to have been assigned under this Act` `the Minister caused the number to be assigned under an agreement with my province`

§§ `Offences and prosecution (sections 102 and 103)`

-- s 102(1).
@export Am I guilty of an offence if I gave false or misleading information in my application for a Social Insurance Number (s 102(1))?
GIVEN `I furnished information in an application for a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you furnish information in an application for a Social Insurance Number?
      `the information was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information false or misleading?
      `I knew it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know it was false or misleading when you furnished it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for false or misleading information in my application for a Social Insurance Number` IS
    `s 102(1) — the person is guilty of an offence for false or misleading information in an application for a Social Insurance Number` `I furnished information in an application for a Social Insurance Number` `the information was false or misleading` `I knew it was false or misleading`

-- s 102(2).
@export Am I guilty of an offence if I applied again for a Social Insurance Number after one was assigned to me (s 102(2))?
GIVEN `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a Social Insurance Number been assigned to you?
      `I made an application again to be assigned a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an application again to be assigned a Social Insurance Number (whether you gave the same information or different information, and whether or not you were assigned one again)?
      `I knew a number had been assigned to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know a number had already been assigned to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for applying again for a Social Insurance Number` IS
    `s 102(2) — the person is guilty of an offence for applying again for a Social Insurance Number` `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to me` `I made an application again to be assigned a Social Insurance Number` `I knew a number had been assigned to me`

@export What is the greatest fine the Act states for an offence under section 102 (s 102)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `cp6 Offence under section 102` @desc Which offence? One of: "furnishing false or misleading information in an application for a Social Insurance Number", "applying again for a Social Insurance Number after one has been assigned", "an employer's failure to comply with subsection 98(5) or a regulation under paragraph 101(1)(a)".
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the greatest fine the Act states for the offence` IS
    `s 102 — the greatest fine the text states for the offence` `the offence`

-- s 103(1).
@export What is the last day on which I could be prosecuted for an offence under the Act (s 103(1))?
GIVEN `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the thing the prosecution would be about arise? (year-month-day)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day on which I could be prosecuted for the offence` IS
    `s 103(1) — the last day on which a prosecution for an offence under this Act may be commenced` `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose`

@export Can I still be prosecuted for an offence under the Act on a given day (s 103(1))?
GIVEN `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the thing the prosecution would be about arise? (year-month-day)
      `the day a prosecution would be commenced` IS A DATE @desc On which day would the prosecution be commenced? (year-month-day)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still be prosecuted for the offence on that day` IS
    `s 103(1) — a prosecution for an offence under this Act may be commenced on a day` `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose` `the day a prosecution would be commenced`

-- s 103(2).
@export Am I a party to and guilty of my corporation's offence under the Act as an officer, director or agent (s 103(2))?
GIVEN `my corporation commits an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation commit an offence under the Act?
      `I am an officer, director or agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer, director or agent of the corporation?
      `what I did` IS A `cp6 Part an officer, director or agent took in the corporation's offence` @desc What part did you take in the offence? One of: "directed the commission of the offence", "authorized the commission of the offence", "assented to the commission of the offence", "acquiesced in the commission of the offence", "participated in the commission of the offence", "took none of those parts".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a party to and guilty of my corporation's offence` IS
    `s 103(2) — the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the corporation's offence` `my corporation commits an offence under the Act` `I am an officer, director or agent of the corporation` `what I did`

-- s 103(3).
@export Does section 41(6) apply to an information or complaint against me under a provision of the Act other than Part I (s 103(3))?
GIVEN `the information or complaint is under a provision of the Act other than Part I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information or complaint made under a provision of the Act other than Part I?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 41(6) apply to the information or complaint against me` IS
    `s 103(3) — subsection 41(6) applies to the information or complaint` `the information or complaint is under a provision of the Act other than Part I`

§§ `Who may see my information; agreements; oaths (sections 104.1 to 107)`

-- s 104.1(1). Information obtained for administering the Act may be passed between named departments despite any other law.
-- Assumed, not ruled: the one yes/no answer (officer or employee of that department, or a person a regulation prescribes) is passed as all three inputs of the public-officer rule
-- (officer or employee; prescribed individual; member of a prescribed class), so any one being true makes the person a public officer, as the definition says.
@export May information about me that was obtained for the administration of the Act be passed from one federal department to another despite any other law (s 104.1(1))?
GIVEN `the department that holds the information` IS A `cp6 Federal body named in section 104.1` @desc Which body holds it? One of: "the Canada Revenue Agency", "the Department of Finance", "the Department of Public Works and Government Services", "the Department of Citizenship and Immigration", "the Department of Employment and Social Development", "the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions", "another body".
      `the person holding it is an officer or employee of that department or a person a regulation prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person holding the information an officer or employee of that department, or someone a regulation prescribes (regulation 37(4))?
      `it was obtained for the purpose of the administration of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it obtained for the purpose of the administration of the Canada Pension Plan Act?
      `the department that would be given the information` IS A `cp6 Federal body named in section 104.1` @desc Which body would be given it? One of the same seven choices.
      `the person who would receive it is an officer or employee of that department or a person a regulation prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who would receive it an officer or employee of that department, or someone a regulation prescribes?
      `it is made available for the purpose of the administration of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made available for the purpose of the administration of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May information about me be passed from one federal department to another` IS
    `s 104.1(1) — the information may be made available despite any other Act or law`
        `the department that holds the information`
        (`s 104(1) — a person is a public officer` `the person holding it is an officer or employee of that department or a person a regulation prescribes` `the person holding it is an officer or employee of that department or a person a regulation prescribes` `the person holding it is an officer or employee of that department or a person a regulation prescribes`)
        `it was obtained for the purpose of the administration of the Act`
        `the department that would be given the information`
        (`s 104(1) — a person is a public officer` `the person who would receive it is an officer or employee of that department or a person a regulation prescribes` `the person who would receive it is an officer or employee of that department or a person a regulation prescribes` `the person who would receive it is an officer or employee of that department or a person a regulation prescribes`)
        `it is made available for the purpose of the administration of the Act`

-- s 104.1(2). It may go no further unless for the same purpose and on the Minister's conditions.
@export May information about me that was obtained under section 104.1 be made available to another person or body (s 104.1(2))?
GIVEN `it was obtained under section 104.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information obtained under section 104.1 of the Act?
      `the person or body is not a public officer of one of the departments named in section 104.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person or body who would receive it someone other than a public officer of one of the departments named in section 104.1(1)?
      `it is made available only for the same purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made available only for the same purpose?
      `it is made available on any conditions the Minister specifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made available on any conditions the Minister specifies (answer yes if the Minister specified none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May information about me obtained under section 104.1 be made available to another person or body` IS
    `s 104.1(2) — the information obtained under section 104.1 may be made available to the other person or body` `it was obtained under section 104.1` `the person or body is not a public officer of one of the departments named in section 104.1(1)` `it is made available only for the same purpose` `it is made available on any conditions the Minister specifies`

-- s 105(a). Under an agreement with my province, my information may go to its pension authority.
@export May information about me obtained under the Act be given to my province's pension plan authority under an agreement (s 105(a))?
GIVEN `an agreement under section 105 is in force with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an agreement under section 105 in force between the Minister and your province's government?
      `the information was obtained under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information obtained under the Canada Pension Plan Act?
      `it is made available under prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made available under the conditions that are prescribed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May information about me be given to my province's pension plan authority` IS
    `s 105(a) — information may be made available under the agreement` `from the Minister to the appropriate authority of the province` `an agreement under section 105 is in force with my province` `the information was obtained under the Act` `it is made available under prescribed conditions` FALSE

-- s 105(b). Under an agreement with my province, I may get my statement of earnings from either authority.
@export May I be given a statement of the earnings shown to my account by my province's pension plan authority instead of the Minister (s 105(b))?
GIVEN `an agreement under section 105 is in force with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an agreement under section 105 in force between the Minister and your province's government?
      `I have made contributions under the Act and under my province's pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made contributions both under the Canada Pension Plan Act and under your province's pension plan?
      `the agreement's terms and conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms and conditions the agreement specifies met?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be given my statement of earnings by my province's pension plan authority` IS
    `s 105(b) — a statement of the amounts shown to the individual's account may be made available by the Minister or the provincial authority` `an agreement under section 105 is in force with my province` `I have made contributions under the Act and under my province's pension plan` `the agreement's terms and conditions are met`

@export May the Minister or my province's authority act on my request to reconsider a statement of my earnings (s 105(b))?
GIVEN `an agreement under section 105 is in force with my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an agreement under section 105 in force between the Minister and your province's government?
      `I have made contributions under the Act and under my province's pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made contributions both under the Canada Pension Plan Act and under your province's pension plan?
      `the agreement's terms and conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms and conditions the agreement specifies met?
      `I have asked for a statement to be reconsidered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked for a statement made available to you to be reconsidered?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister or my province's authority act on my request to reconsider a statement` IS
    `s 105(b) — the Minister or the provincial authority may act on the individual's request for reconsideration` `an agreement under section 105 is in force with my province` `I have made contributions under the Act and under my province's pension plan` `the agreement's terms and conditions are met` `I have asked for a statement to be reconsidered`

-- s 106(1). An official authorized by a Minister may take my oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation for the Act's purposes.
@export May the official take my oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation for the purposes of the Act (s 106(1))?
GIVEN `the official's employment` IS A `cp6 Employee authorized to take oaths for the Act` @desc Which is the official? One of: "employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue", "employed in the administration or enforcement of Part III and Part II or their regulations and authorized by the Minister", "neither of those".
      `the official acts in the course of their employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the official acting in the course of their employment?
      `another Act of Parliament or of a provincial legislature limits the official's power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another Act of Parliament or an Act of a provincial legislature limit the official's power to take it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the official take my oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` IS
    `s 106(1) — the authorized person may administer oaths, take affidavits, declarations and solemn affirmations, and has the powers of a commissioner for taking affidavits` `the official's employment` `the official acts in the course of their employment` `another Act of Parliament or of a provincial legislature limits the official's power`

-- s 107(1)(b), (c). An agreement with another country may extend, increase or decrease the benefits payable to a person employed or resident in either country.
@export May an agreement with another country provide for my benefits to be extended, increased or decreased (s 107(1))?
GIVEN `an agreement between Canada and another country under section 107 is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an agreement between Canada and another country under section 107(1) in force?
      `I am employed in or resident in the other country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in or resident in the other country?
      `I am employed in or resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in or resident in Canada?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May an agreement with another country provide for my benefits to be extended, increased or decreased` IS
    `s 107(1)(b) and (c) — the agreement may provide for the benefits payable to or in respect of the person to be extended, increased or decreased` `an agreement between Canada and another country under section 107 is in force` `I am employed in or resident in the other country` `I am employed in or resident in Canada`

§§ `Gifts to the Minister (a situational group: only if you are giving the Minister money or property)`

-- s 107.1.
@export If I give the Minister securities or other property on terms, must the Minister dispose of it subject to those terms (s 107.1)?
GIVEN `what I give is securities or other property, not money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you give securities or other property (not money)?
      `I stated terms on which I give it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you state terms on which you give it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister dispose of what I give subject to my terms` IS
    `s 107.1 — the Minister must dispose of the property subject to the terms on which it was made available` `what I give is securities or other property, not money` `I stated terms on which I give it`

§§ `My contribution, and the rates (sections 108, 113.1, 114 and Schedules 1 and 2)`

-- s 108(2)(a), 108.2(2)(a).
@export Into which account of Canada is my contribution credited (s 108(2)(a), 108.2(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the kind of my contribution` IS A Tier @desc Which contribution? One of: "the base tier" (the base contribution), "the first additional tier" (the first additional contribution, from 2019), "the second additional tier" (the second additional contribution, from 2024).
GIVETH A `cp6 Account of Canada under the Act`
DECIDE `Into which account of Canada is my contribution credited` IS
    `s 108(2)(a) and 108.2(2)(a) — the account to which a contribution of a tier is credited` `the kind of my contribution`

-- Schedules 1 and 2.
@export What contribution rate do Schedules 1 and 2 set for me for a year (Schedules 1 and 2)?
GIVEN `the kind of contribution` IS A Tier @desc Which contribution? One of: "the base tier", "the first additional tier" (from 2019), "the second additional tier" (from 2024).
      `I contribute as` IS A `Contributing capacity` @desc In which capacity do you contribute? One of: "contributing as an employee", "contributing as an employer", "contributing as a self-employed person".
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc For which calendar year? (for example 2026)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What contribution rate do the Schedules set for me for the year` IS
    `Schedule 1 and 2 — the contribution rate of a tier and a capacity for a year` `the kind of contribution` `I contribute as` `the year`

-- s 113.1(7). Limits on a change of the rates for a year.
@export Is a change of the contribution rates for a year within the limits the Act sets (s 113.1(7))?
GIVEN `the rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.0495 for 4.95 per cent)?
      `the rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate for employers for the year, as a fraction?
      `the rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate for self-employed persons for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.099)?
      `the rate for employees for the previous year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the rate for employees for the previous year, as a fraction?
      `the rate for employers for the previous year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the rate for employers for the previous year, as a fraction?
      `the rate for self-employed persons for the previous year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the rate for self-employed persons for the previous year, as a fraction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the change of the contribution rates for the year within the limits` IS
    `s 113.1(7) — the setting of the rates for the year is within the limits` `the rate for employees for the year` `the rate for employers for the year` `the rate for self-employed persons for the year` `the rate for employees for the previous year` `the rate for employers for the previous year` `the rate for self-employed persons for the previous year`

-- s 113.1(8). When a regulation changing the rates comes into force.
@export When does a regulation changing the contribution rates come into force (s 113.1(8))?
GIVEN `the first year of the three-year period` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year does the three-year review period begin? (the first begins in 1998, then every third year: 2001, 2004, ... 2025, 2028)
      `the day the Governor in Council made the regulation` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Governor in Council make the regulation changing the rates? (year-month-day)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `When does a regulation changing the contribution rates come into force` IS
    `s 113.1(8) — the day the regulation comes into force` `the first year of the three-year period` `the day the Governor in Council made the regulation`

-- s 113.1(11.05) and (11.13). When the rates are found insufficient the schedule is deemed amended.
@export Are the contribution rates found insufficient, so that Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended (s 113.1(11.05))?
GIVEN `the rate for self-employed persons for the years in the three-year period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate for self-employed persons for the years in the three-year period, at October 1 of the year before, as a fraction (for example 0.099)?
      `the rate most recently calculated for the changes under paragraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii) (the Chief Actuary's rate for the changes), as a fraction?
      `the rate most recently calculated under paragraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i) (the Chief Actuary's rate for self-employed persons), as a fraction?
      `a recommendation to increase the rates was made in the three years before the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the three years before the period, was it recommended that the rates be increased?
      `the rates were increased before October 1 of the year before the period to give effect to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the rates increased before October 1 of the year before the period, by an Act of Parliament or a regulation, to give effect to it?
      `a recommendation not to increase the rates was made in the three years before the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the three years before the period, was it recommended that the rates not be increased?
      `the Minister of Finance had that recommendation published in the Canada Gazette before October 1 of the year before the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister of Finance have that recommendation published in the Canada Gazette before October 1 of the year before the period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the contribution rates found insufficient, so that Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended` IS
    `s 113.1(11.05) — Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended`
        (`s 113.1(11.05) — the rate for self-employed persons is insufficient` `the rate for self-employed persons for the years in the three-year period` `the rate most recently calculated for the changes under paragraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` `the rate most recently calculated under paragraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)`)
        (`s 113.1(11.13) — subsection 113.1(11.05) does not apply` `a recommendation to increase the rates was made in the three years before the period` `the rates were increased before October 1 of the year before the period to give effect to it` `a recommendation not to increase the rates was made in the three years before the period` `the Minister of Finance had that recommendation published in the Canada Gazette before October 1 of the year before the period`)

-- s 113.1(11.06) to (11.14). The rate that applies to me after the deemed amendment.
@export What contribution rate applies to me for a year after the rates are deemed amended as insufficient (s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14))?
GIVEN `I contribute as` IS A `Contributing capacity` @desc In which capacity do you contribute? One of: "contributing as an employee", "contributing as an employer", "contributing as a self-employed person".
      `the rate most recently calculated under paragraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i) (the Chief Actuary's rate for self-employed persons), as a fraction (for example 0.10 for 10 per cent)?
      `the rate most recently calculated for the changes under paragraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii), as a fraction (0 if none)?
      `the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last period for which rates were set` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set, as a fraction (for example 0.0495)?
      `the number of the year after the October 1 date` IS A NUMBER @desc Which year after the October 1 date? 1 for the first year, 2 for the next, 3 or more for each later year.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What contribution rate applies to me for the year after the rates are deemed amended` IS
    CONSIDER `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) — the contribution rate for employees and employers for the year, as rounded` `the rate most recently calculated under paragraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` `the rate most recently calculated for the changes under paragraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` `the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last period for which rates were set` `the number of the year after the October 1 date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rate THEN
        CONSIDER `I contribute as`
        WHEN `contributing as an employee` THEN JUST rate
        WHEN `contributing as an employer` THEN JUST rate
        WHEN `contributing as a self-employed person` THEN JUST (`s 113.1(11.05)(b)(ii) — the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` rate)

-- s 113(1)(a). When a province takes over the plan's accrued obligations, the Act stops owing the benefits attributable to contributions made there.
@export Has the Act stopped owing the benefits attributable to my contributions in a province that has taken over the plan (s 113(1)(a))?
GIVEN `a regulation prescribes my province as one that has assumed the accrued obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a regulation been made under section 3(2) prescribing your province as a province described in paragraph (b) of the definition of "province providing a comprehensive pension plan"?
      `my province made provision by law for the assumption of the accrued obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a law of your province made provision for the assumption, under its plan, of the obligations and liabilities accrued or accruing as that paragraph describes?
      `the benefit is attributable to contributions I made in that province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit attributable to contributions made under the Act in respect of employment in that province, or to your self-employed earnings while resident there?
      `the date my province gave written notice` IS A DATE @desc On which day did your province's government give written notice under section 3 (year-month-day)?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask? (year-month-day)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Act stopped owing the benefit attributable to my contributions in my province` IS
    `s 113(1)(a) — the obligation or liability ceases to be one with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act` `a regulation prescribes my province as one that has assumed the accrued obligations` `my province made provision by law for the assumption of the accrued obligations` `the benefit is attributable to contributions I made in that province` `the date my province gave written notice` `the day I ask about`

-- s 114(2). A change in the general level of benefits or in a contribution rate may take effect no earlier than the first day of the third year after notice.
@export What is the earliest day an Act of Parliament changing the general level of benefits or the contribution rates may come into force (s 114(2))?
GIVEN `the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year was the notice of intention to introduce the measure laid before Parliament? (for example 2026)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the earliest day the change may come into force` IS
    `s 114(2) — the earliest day on which the provision may come into force` `the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament`

@export May a provision of an Act of Parliament changing the general level of benefits or the contribution rates come into force on a given day (s 114(2))?
GIVEN `the provision alters the general level of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision alter the general level of benefits provided by the Act, directly or indirectly, now or in the future?
      `the provision alters a contribution rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision alter the contribution rate, the first additional contribution rate or the second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year?
      `the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year was the notice of intention laid before Parliament?
      `the day is fixed by order of the Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council?
      `the day the provision would come into force` IS A DATE @desc On which day would the provision come into force? (year-month-day)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the provision come into force on that day` IS
    `s 114(2) — the provision may come into force on a day` `an enactment of Parliament` `the provision alters the general level of benefits` `the provision alters a contribution rate` `the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament` `the day is fixed by order of the Governor in Council` `the day the provision would come into force`

-- s 114(4). Other changes of substance need the consent of two thirds of the included provinces.
@export Does an Act of Parliament that changes benefits, rates or formulae need the consent of the provinces before it comes into force (s 114(4))?
GIVEN `what the provision alters` IS A `cp6 Matter an enactment of Parliament alters for subsection 114(4)` @desc What does the provision alter? One of: "the general level of benefits provided by the Act", "the classes of benefits provided by the Act", "the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year", "the formulae for calculating the contributions and benefits payable under the Act", "the management or operation of the Canada Pension Plan Account or the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account", "the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act", "some other matter".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act of Parliament need the consent of the provinces` IS
    `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `an enactment of Parliament` `what the provision alters`
